<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Two entitlements, and BOTH are load-bearing. Rationale, and the one
  entitlement deliberately ABSENT, are in FINDINGS.md under "Entitlements".

  Keep prose here short and free of double-hyphens: AMFI parses this file with
  its own XML reader, a double-hyphen is illegal inside an XML comment, and the
  failure is `AMFIUnserializeXML: syntax error`, after which NOTHING embeds.
  That reproduces the exact symptom of the MH_BUNDLE bug for an unrelated
  reason, which is a bad trap to leave in a file about not leaving such traps.

  com.apple.security.application-groups MUST list exactly the string that
  Info-appex.plist gives for NSExtensionFileProviderDocumentGroup. Omitting it
  does not fail loudly: `codesign` is happy, `pluginkit` lists the extension,
  and only `fileproviderd` says why, once, at ERROR level:

      Extension ... doesn't have a group container for document group
      group.kr.swjeon.shepherd.spike specified via
      NSExtensionFileProviderDocumentGroup. Ignoring the extension.

  The caller sees `-2014 ApplicationExtensionNotFound`, which reads as "your
  extension was never discovered" when in fact it was discovered and then
  discarded. Verified 2026-08-19 on host and in a fresh VM. See FINDINGS.md.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key><true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
  <array><string>group.kr.swjeon.shepherd.spike</string></array>
</dict>
</plist>
